-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Core — MIT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything in this repository is MIT-licensed (see `LICENSE`) **except** the
seLe4n-integration components listed in section 2. The MIT core comprises:

  * crates/topo-core, topo-abi, topo-backend-posix, topo-arch, topo-stats,
    topo-control, topo-test-support
  * tools/size-class-gen, tools/trace-replay
  * xtask, tests (the test crate's own sources)
  * lean/TopoMalloc/** except the SeLe4n bridge (section 2)
  * include/** and all generated artifacts

The default, distributable TopoMalloc artifact (`libtopomalloc`, the POSIX
backend) is built **without** any GPL component and is therefore MIT-licensed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. seLe4n integration — GPL-3.0-or-later
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The seLe4n-integration components are licensed GPL-3.0-or-later (see
`sele4n/LICENSE`), because they link or model the GPLv3 seLe4n microkernel ABI
(`hatter6822/seLe4n`, pinned per decision D8). They are:

  * crates/topo-backend-sele4n  — Sele4nSim and (from M1) the Sele4nBackingProvider
  * lean/TopoMalloc/SeLe4n/**   — the Lean bridge model
  * sele4n/**                   — the resource-server component and adapters

Building TopoMalloc with the `sele4n-sim` Cargo feature (e.g.
`libtopomalloc-sele4n`) links these GPL components; the resulting combined
binary is therefore GPL-3.0-or-later. The MIT crates' own source files are
unchanged and remain MIT; only the combined work is GPL.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. SPDX policy (W0-12)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every source file carries an `SPDX-License-Identifier` header:

  * `MIT`                — core files
  * `GPL-3.0-or-later`   — the section-2 seLe4n-integration files

CI enforces this (`cargo xtask lint`). When adding a file under
`crates/topo-backend-sele4n`, `lean/TopoMalloc/SeLe4n`, or `sele4n/`, use the
`GPL-3.0-or-later` identifier; everywhere else use `MIT`.

